Algorithm: Forward Chaining

Start

1. Initialize the known facts.
2. Initialize the set of rules.
3. Repeat
      a. Select a rule whose condition is satisfied.
      b. If the conclusion is not already a known fact,
            i. Add the conclusion to the facts.
            ii. Display the newly derived fact.
4. Continue until no new facts can be derived.
5. Display all final facts.

Stop
